<title>RUSSIA: Russia ups 96 titanium exports 43 pct to 27,920 T.</title>
<headline>Russia ups 96 titanium exports 43 pct to 27,920 T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia exported 27,920 tonnes of titanium and articles containing titanium in 1996 to all destinations, 43 percent more than in 1995, State Customs Committee figures showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The figures, quoted by Interfax news agency, showed Ireland as the largest buyer, importing 5,980 tonnes.</p>
<p>The United States imported 5,150 tonnes, the Netherlands 5,090 tonnes, Germany 3,250 tonnes, Italy 2,160 tonnes and Japan 1,600 tonnes.</p>
<p>Interfax also said Russia's biggest titanium fabricator, the Verkhnaya Salda Metallurgical Production Association, produced 5,000 tonnes of titanium products in 1996. It is the world's largest producer of titanium alloys.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
